     "scene_010": {
       "title": "Jump onto the Bot",
-      "text": "\n“Ok, you've got this,” you say as you prep yourself.\n\nYou take three running steps across the garage roof and jump, and you land right on top of the Construction Bot’s big round head with a CLANG that rattles your teeth. The bot fires its foot thrusters and starts hopping all over the street, trying to shake you off.\n\n“Sir!” Asher shouts from the garage speakers. “That is not a recognized safety procedure!”\n\n“YOU THINK?!?”\n\nYou hang on with one hand, jam the prybar end of The Can Opener under the panel behind its head, and lean on it with everything you’ve got. The panel pops off!\n\nInside is a nest of wires and one fat cable labeled MAIN POWER. Thank you, whoever labels things.\n\nYou clamp the wrench jaws around it and pull. The thrusters cut out, the bot sits down with a THUNK, and its eyes fade from angry red to a soft blue before going dark.\n\nYou slide off its head and land on some very shaky legs.\n\nTool first, weapon second, just like you planned it…mostly.\n",
+      "text": "\n“Ok, you’ve got this,” you say as you prepare yourself.\n\nYou take three running steps across the garage roof and jump, landing right on top of the Construction Bot’s big round head with a CLANG that rattles your whole body. The bot fires its foot thrusters and starts hopping all over the street, trying to shake you off.\n\n“Sir!” Asher shouts from the garage speakers. “That is not a recognized safety procedure!”\n\n“OH REALLY?!?”\n\nYou hang on with one hand, jam the prybar end of The Can Opener under the panel behind its head, and lean on it with everything you’ve got. The panel pops off!\n\nInside is a nest of wires and one fat cable labeled MAIN POWER. Thank you, whoever labels these things.\n\nYou jam the wrench’s prybar behind the wire and pull with all your strength. The thrusters cut out, the bot falls down with a THUNK, and its eyes fade from angry red to a soft blue before going dark.\n\nYou slide off onto the pavement, legs shaking.\n\nYou look at The Can Opener and think to yourself, this thing is like a giant Swiss Army knife. It’s perfect.\n",
