-      "text": "\n“Welcome back, sir,” Asher says. “The deep diagnostic on our first bot still has hours to go. However, I have found something early.”\n\nA wall of code scrolls across the screen, and one chunk of it is highlighted in red.\n\n“This is the strange code from the storage drives. It is also inside the bot you brought home. Same code, same spot, every single time.”\n\n“So it’s a glitch that keeps happening?”\n\n“That is the odd part, sir. Glitches are messy. This is tidy. It looks less like something that broke and more like something that was added.”\n\nYou stare at the red block of code. Somebody did this? On PURPOSE? To robots that were just supposed to fix roads and carry boxes?\n\n“Keep digging,” you say. “I want to know what it does.”\n\n“Understood, sir. In the meantime, may I point out that there will probably be more of them?”\n\nYeah. He’s right. You need to be ready.\n",
+      "text": "\n“Welcome back, sir,” Asher says. “The deep diagnostic on our first bot still has hours to go. However, I have found something already.”\n\nA wall of code scrolls across the screen, and one chunk of it is highlighted in red.\n\n“This is the strange code from the storage drives. It is also inside the bot you brought home. I am finding it on every bot you bring in.”\n\n“So is it a glitch, or did someone put it there?”\n\n“That is the odd part, sir. Glitches are messy. This isn’t. It looks less like something that broke and more like something that was added.”\n\nYou stare at the red block of code. Somebody did this! On PURPOSE? To robots that were just supposed to fix roads and carry boxes?\n\n“Keep digging,” you say. “I want to know what it does. And good job, Asher.”\n\n“Thank you, sir. I will keep looking, but in the meantime, may I point out that there will probably be more of them?”\n\nHe’s right. You need to be ready.\n",
