     "scene_013": {
       "title": "Survey the Destroyed Bot",
-      "text": "\nYou crouch down next to the Construction Bot and take a good look.\n\nUp close it doesn’t look scary at all, it just looks old. The white paint is chipped, one of its foot thrusters is patched with a totally different color, and somebody once stuck a smiley face sticker on its tool cabinet. The sticker’s half peeled off, and with those angry eyebrows above it, the bot looks like it’s having the worst day of its whole life.\n\nThis bot fixed potholes for years. It didn’t ask to go haywire.\n\n“Sorry, big guy,” you say quietly.\n\nOn its side you find a metal tag where the owner’s name should be, except it’s been scratched off. Not worn off…scratched, with a tool, on purpose. You pry the tag loose and stick it in your pocket.\n\nAcross the street, a curtain moves in the window above Mrs. Ruiz’s market. Somebody saw that whole fight!\n\nYou pull your goggles down over your eyes and turn your face away. You’re not doing this to get famous. Time to get off the street.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou crouch down next to the Construction Bot and take a good look.\n\nUp close it doesn’t look scary at all, it just looks old. The white paint is chipped, one of its foot thrusters is patched with a totally different color, and somebody once stuck a smiley face sticker on its tool cabinet. The sticker’s half peeled off, and with those angry eyebrows above it, the bot looks like it’s having the worst day of its whole life.\n\nThis bot fixed potholes for years. We need to figure out why they are going haywire.\n\n“Sorry, big guy,” you say quietly.\n\nOn its side you find a metal tag where the owner’s name should be, except it’s been scraped off. Not worn off…scraped. You pry the tag loose and stick it in your pocket.\n\nAcross the street, a curtain moves in the window above Mrs. Ruiz’s market. Somebody saw that whole fight!\n\nYou pull your goggles down over your eyes and turn your face away. If you learned anything from comic books, it’s that a secret identity is important. Time to get back inside.\n",
