-      "text": "\nYou grab your backpack and head out into {world_name}.\n\nThe Construction Bot in the street gives up some good parts: a handful of heavy springs, a piston from one of its foot thrusters, and a length of steel tube. You apologize to it again while you work. It just seems like the polite thing to do.\n\nYou keep going, all the way to the loading zone behind Mrs. Ruiz’s market, and that’s where you see it.\n\nA Load-Bot. It’s built like three big crates stacked on top of each other, with a square head, forklift prongs for hands, and big round rolling wheels instead of feet. There’s a screen on its chest with a little progress bar that says 87%. And painted on its face is a great big smile.\n\nIt’s picking up crates of oranges and watermelons and throwing them at a wall, one after another, smiling the whole time.\n\nIts eyes are the same flickering red.\n\nIt hasn’t noticed you yet, and your backpack is already full of exactly the parts you need.\n",
