     "scene_019": {
       "title": "Close Call",
-      "text": "\nYou creep along the fence to get a better look.\n\nThe Load-Bot is slow. Like, REALLY slow. But when it scoops up a crate, the wood creaks on its forklift prongs, and when it throws one, the crate explodes into splinters and oranges. The progress bar on its chest ticks up to 88%. You really don’t want to know what happens at 100.\n\nSlow but strong. Got it.\n\nYou take one more step, and your foot lands on a rolling orange. You don’t fall…but you do yell “WHOA,” which is just as bad.\n\nThe Load-Bot turns its big smiling face toward you and picks up a crate.\n\n“Run, sir,” Asher’s voice says from your phone. “That is my whole plan. Run.”\n\nSo you RUN. A crate smashes into the fence right behind you, and another one bursts on the pavement right where you were standing a second ago. You don’t stop until you’re back in the garage with the door shut.\n\nOk. The Can Opener only works if you’re close enough to touch the bot, and you do NOT want to be anywhere near those forklift hands.\n\nYou really, really need something with range.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou creep along the fence to get a better look.\n\nThe Load-Bot is slow. Like, REALLY slow. But when it scoops up a crate, the wood creaks on its forklift prongs, and when it throws one, the crate explodes into splinters and oranges. The progress bar on its chest ticks up to 88%. You really don’t want to know what happens at 100.\n\nSlow but strong. Got it.\n\nYou take one more step, and your foot lands on a rolling orange. You don’t fall…but you do yell “WHOA.”\n\nThe Load-Bot turns its big smiling face toward you and picks up a crate.\n\n“Run, sir,” Asher’s voice says from your phone.\n\n“Run? You think?”\n\nAnd you RUN. A crate smashes into the fence right behind you, and another one bursts on the pavement right where you were standing a second ago. You don’t stop until you’re back in the garage with the door shut.\n\nOk. The Can Opener only works if you’re close enough to touch the bot, and you do NOT want to be anywhere near those forklift hands.\n\nYou really, really need something for distance.\n",
