     "scene_021": {
       "title": "More Power",
-      "text": "\nMore power fixes everything. Probably.\n\nYou double the springs, add a second coil, and wire the whole thing straight into a spare power cell, and you skip the part where you test it on low.\n\n“Sir, I would like it noted that I asked you to test it on low.”\n\n“Noted!”\n\nYou aim at the paint can and press the trigger.\n\nThe rock doesn’t come out the front. The ENTIRE launcher rips off your arm, flies backward across the garage, and sticks in the wall like a dart. The paint can hasn’t moved an inch.\n\nYou stand there with an empty wrist brace and your hair sticking straight up.\n\n“Ok,” you say. “Less power.”\n\n“And perhaps some bolts, sir.”\n\n“And some bolts.”\n\nThis time you do it right. You bolt the barrel to the brace, flip the coil (which turns out to have been in backwards the whole time), take the extra springs back out, and add a piston to smooth out the push.\n",
+      "text": "\nMore power fixes everything. Right?\n\nYou double the springs, add a second coil, and wire the whole thing straight into a spare power cell, and you skip the part where you test it on low.\n\n“Sir, I would like it noted that I asked you to test it on low.”\n\n“Noted!”\n\nYou aim at the paint can and press the trigger.\n\nThe rock doesn’t come out the front. The ENTIRE launcher rips off your arm, flies backward across the garage, and sticks in the wall like a dart. The paint can hasn’t moved an inch.\n\nYou stand there with an empty wrist brace and your hair sticking straight up.\n\n“Ok,” you say. “Less power.”\n\n“And perhaps some bolts, sir.”\n\n“And some bolts.”\n\nThis time you don’t rush it. You look at your blueprint and see what you missed. You bolt the barrel to the brace, flip the coil (which turns out to have been in backwards the whole time), take the extra springs back out, and add a piston to smooth out the push.\n",
