     "scene_027": {
       "title": "Two Tools, One Win",
-      "text": "\nYou circle around behind the fallen Load-Bot, staying clear of those arms. There…a panel on its back!\n\nYou jam the prybar end of The Can Opener under the edge and lean on it until the panel pops, then reach in with the wrench jaws, find the main power cable, and PULL.\n\nThe arms stop. Its eyes fade from red to soft blue, then go dark, and the progress bar on its chest drops all the way back to 0%.\n\nYou let out a long breath.\n\n“Two tools, one win, sir,” Asher says. “I believe that is what they call a loadout.”\n\nThe dented back door of the market creaks open, and Mrs. Ruiz peeks out holding a broom like a sword. She looks at the bot. Then she looks at you, with your goggles down and a glowing thing on your wrist.\n\n“Whoever you are,” she calls, “thank you!”\n\nYou freeze. You were really hoping nobody would see you.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou circle around behind the fallen Load-Bot, staying clear of its arms. There…a panel on its back!\n\nYou jam the prybar end of The Can Opener under the edge and lean on it until the panel pops, then reach in with the wrench jaws, find the main power cable, and PULL.\n\nThe arms stop. Its eyes fade from red to soft blue, then go dark, and the progress bar on its chest drops all the way to 0% before fading entirely.\n\nYou let out a long breath.\n\n“Two tools, one win, sir,” Asher says. “I believe that is what they call a loadout.”\n\nThe dented back door of the market creaks open, and Mrs. Ruiz peeks out holding a broom like a sword. She looks at the bot. Then she looks at you, with your goggles down and a glowing thing on your wrist.\n\n“Whoever you are,” she calls, “thank you!”\n\nYou freeze. You were really hoping nobody would see you.\n",
