     "scene_028": {
       "title": "The Shopkeeper",
-      "text": "\nYou keep your goggles on and your voice low, which makes you sound like you have a cold.\n\n“Are you ok, ma’am?”\n\n“I’m fine. My watermelons are not.” Mrs. Ruiz lowers the broom. “That’s the third robot this month. Nobody comes when we call. They say {world_name} isn’t a priority.”\n\nShe shakes her head.\n\n“And then that man shows up. Shiny suit, big smile, too many teeth. He says the neighborhood has gone downhill. He says he’ll buy my store, but for almost nothing, because who else would want it now?”\n\nShe snorts.\n\n“I told him I’d think about it. I did think about it. The answer is no.”\n\nA man in a shiny suit, buying up stores for cheap, right after the robots show up? Hmm. You tuck that away for later.\n\nMrs. Ruiz ducks inside and comes back out with a juice box.\n\n“Heroes need to stay hydrated,” she says, and pushes it into your hand.\n\nYou blush as you take a long sip on the juice box.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou keep your goggles on and your voice low, which makes you sound like you have a cold.\n\n“Are you ok, ma’am?”\n\n“I’m fine, thanks to you. My fruit, well, it’s too bad I don’t run a smoothie shop.” Mrs. Ruiz lowers the broom. “That’s the third robot this month. Nobody comes when we call. They say {world_name} isn’t a priority.”\n\nShe shakes her head.\n\n“And then that man shows up. Gold shiny suit, big toothy smile. He says the neighborhood has gone downhill. He asked to buy my store, for almost nothing, because who else would want it now?”\n\nShe snorts.\n\n“I told him I’d think about it. I didn’t think about it, though. The answer is always no. Wait there for a second.”\n\nA man in a shiny suit, buying up stores for cheap, right after the robots show up? Hmm. You tuck that away for later.\n\nMrs. Ruiz ducks inside and comes back out with a juice box.\n\n“Heroes need to stay hydrated,” she says as she hands it to you.\n\n“Thank you,” you say, blushing as you take a long sip on the juice box.\n",
