-      "text": "\nBack in the garage, you open the big door to let some air in and put the shield prototype up on the workbench.\n\nIt’s still ugly, it’s still unstable, and it’s still held together with way more tape than you’d like to admit. You’ve got it half taken apart, with the emitter in one hand and a screwdriver in the other, when Asher speaks up.\n\n“Sir. Something is coming up the driveway.”\n\nYou look up.\n\nIt’s smaller than the other bots and way faster. It’s boxy and white, with big round eyes, a grille for a mouth, and a yellow bulb on a little antenna that blinks the whole time. One hand is a wrench. The other one is holding a taser stick that crackles and sparks. It rolls around on little wheels, and MALL SECURITY is still stenciled across its chest.\n\nA Close Range Security Bot. Its round eyes flicker red.\n\nIt rolls right into the garage and parks itself between you and the rest of the room. The Can Opener is on the desk on the far side, The Wrist Wrock-It is on the charger next to it, and the only thing within reach is a half-built shield.\n",
