     "scene_035": {
       "title": "The Same Fingerprints",
-      "text": "\nYou plug the Security Bot into Asher and wait. It doesn’t take long.\n\n“Same code, sir. The same red block, in the same spot, as the Construction Bot and every drive you have brought home. But this one was not broken down in a junk pile. It was running. So I can see something new.”\n\nA line of numbers pops up on the screen, ticking upward.\n\n“The code is listening. Several times a second, it checks for something from outside. Instructions, I think. This bot did not wander into our garage, sir. Something told it where to go.”\n\n“Something told it where to go? That’s bad, Asher…very bad.”\n\n“Can you tell where it’s coming from?”\n\n“Not from here. The garage walls block too much, and whatever it is, it is faint. I would need to be out there, close to a bot while it is still running.”\n\nYou look at Asher’s big computer tower. It weighs more than you do.\n\n“That’s gonna be a problem.”\n\n“Yes, sir. It is.”\n\nBefore bed, you bolt the loose emitter into the armband, secure the power pack to its side, and tape the wiring down. You add a switch beside your left wrist so you can turn it on without reaching under the tape. This time the shield holds steady for forty seconds before the pack gets warm. You shut it off, but your mind is still running through everything that happened tonight.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou plug the Security Bot into Asher and wait. It doesn’t take long.\n\n“Same code, sir. The same red block, in the same spot, as the Construction Bot and every drive you have brought home. But this one was not broken down in a junk pile. It was running. So I can see something new.”\n\nA line of numbers pops up on the screen, ticking upward.\n\n“The code is listening. Several times a second, it checks for something from outside. Instructions, I think. This bot did not wander into our garage, sir. Something told it where to go.”\n\n“Something told it where to go? That’s really not good, Asher. Can you tell where it’s coming from?”\n\n“Not from here. The garage walls block too much, and whatever it is, it is faint. I would need to be out there, close to a bot while it is still running.”\n\nYou look at Asher’s big computer tower. It weighs more than you do.\n\n“That’s gonna be a problem.”\n\n“Yes, sir. It is.”\n\nBefore bed, you bolt the loose emitter into the shield armband, secure the power pack to its side, and tape the wiring down. You add a switch beside your left wrist so you can turn it on without reaching under the tape. This time the shield holds steady for forty seconds before the pack gets warm. You shut it off, but your mind is still running through everything that happened tonight.\n",
