         "reinforced": "\nThe next afternoon, you head out with all three inventions for the first time. You feel ready for anything!\n",
         "analyzed": "\nThe next afternoon, you head out with all three inventions for the first time. If something is sending these bots, you want to see where they go.\n"
       },
-      "text": "\nMr. Lin is on his bench at the top of Main Street, where he always is, with a coffee in one hand and nothing in the other.\n\nHe looks at The Can Opener on your belt. He looks at the duct-taped armband on your left arm. He looks at the launcher on your right. Then he looks back at his coffee.\n\n“Afternoon.”\n\n“Afternoon, Mr. Lin.”\n\nThere’s a gold flyer taped to the bench beside him: A GIFT FROM GAS! WE’RE BUYING! ASK US HOW!\n\n“You’re keeping that?”\n\n“That’s going in a frame.” He takes a sip. “Guy in a shiny suit handed it to me. Talked for forty minutes. Never asked me one question. Lot of hot air.”\n\nA gold truck rolls past with GAS painted on the side in letters as tall as you are. Its horn plays a little song.\n\n“And GAS,” Mr. Lin says.\n\nYou have no idea what GAS is, and you decide you don’t want to know.\n\n“We still on for hoops Saturday?”\n\n“If you’re not busy.” He nods at your belt. “Looks like you might be busy.”\n\n“I’ll make time.”\n\n“Good. I need the practice.”\n\nHe does not need the practice.\n\nYou keep walking, and you’re halfway down Main Street when a bright bolt of light zips past your ear and hits the bus stop sign behind you. The sign goes numb. You didn’t even know a sign could do that!\n\nYou dive behind a big blue mailbox.\n\nUp on the roof of the old bank, three stories up, is a tall, skinny bot with a long oval head, angry eyebrows, and a dark visor where its eyes should be. It’s standing on roller-skate wheels and pointing a taser blaster down at the street…and for some reason, its other hand is giving you a thumbs-up. PERIMETER DEFENSE is stenciled on its chest, and its visor flickers red.\n\nA Long Range Security Bot.\n\nZAP! Another stun bolt hits the mailbox, and your fingers tingle right through the metal.\n\n“Sir, it has the high ground and a clear view of the whole street,” Asher says from your phone. “The Can Opener cannot reach it. I am not sure you can reach it.”\n\nEvery time you peek out, it fires. And every time, that thumb stays up.\n",
+      "text": "\nMr. Lin is on his bench at the top of Main Street, where he always is, with a coconut water in one hand and nothing in the other.\n\nHe looks at The Can Opener on your belt. He looks at the duct-taped armband on your left arm. He looks at the launcher on your right. Then he looks back at his coconut water.\n\n“Afternoon.”\n\n“Afternoon, Mr. Lin.”\n\nThere’s a gold flyer taped to the bench beside him: A GIFT FROM GAS! WE’RE BUYING! ASK US HOW!\n\n“You’re keeping that?”\n\n“That’s going in a frame.” He takes a sip. “Guy in a shiny suit handed it to me. Talked for forty minutes. Never asked me one question. Lots of hot air.”\n\nA gold truck rolls past with GAS painted on the side in letters as tall as you are. Its horn plays a little song.\n\n“And GAS,” Mr. Lin says.\n\nYou have no idea what GAS is, and you decide you don’t want to know.\n\n“We still on for hoops Saturday?”\n\n“If you’re not busy.” He nods at your belt. “Looks like you might be busy.”\n\n“I’ll make time.”\n\n“Good. I need the practice.”\n\nHe does not need the practice.\n\nYou keep walking, and you’re halfway down Main Street when a bright bolt of light zips past your ear and hits the bus stop sign behind you. The sign goes numb. You didn’t even know a sign could do that!\n\nYou dive behind a big blue mailbox.\n\nUp on the roof of the old bank, three stories up, is a tall, skinny bot with a long oval head, angry eyebrows, and a dark visor where its eyes should be. It’s standing on roller-skate wheels and pointing a taser blaster down at the street…and for some reason, its other hand is giving you a thumbs-up.\n\nA Long Range Security Bot.\n\nZAP! Another stun bolt hits the mailbox, and your fingers tingle right through the metal.\n\n“Sir, it has the high ground and a clear view of the whole street,” Asher says from your phone. “The Can Opener cannot reach it. I am not sure you can reach it.”\n\nEvery time you peek out, it fires. And every time, you see the weird thumbs-up.\n",
