-      "text": "\nYou open the garage door and step out into the evening, and Asher doesn’t say anything for almost a full minute.\n\n“Sir,” he finally says, very quietly. “The sky is so much bigger than the camera made it look.”\n\nYou let him look for a while.\n\nThen the little blue ring in your vision blinks, and a box draws itself around something high above the rooftops.\n\n“Sir. Two o’clock, high. Do you see that?”\n\nYou squint. A tiny blinking light, hanging perfectly still in the sky.\n\n“It’s that drone! I saw it from the roof before.”\n\n“It is not a delivery drone, sir. Those move. This one has been in that exact spot since we came outside. It is watching the neighborhood.”\n\nYou would’ve walked right under it. You HAVE walked right under it, who knows how many times.\n\n“Good eyes, Asher.”\n\n“They are your eyes, sir. I am only borrowing one.”\n\nThe drone is way too high to reach…for now. One more thing to build.\n",
+      "text": "\nYou open the garage door and step out into the evening, and Asher doesn’t say anything for almost a full minute.\n\n“Sir,” he finally says, very quietly. “The sky is so much bigger than the camera made it look.”\n\nYou let him look for a while.\n\nThen the little blue ring in your vision blinks, and a box draws itself around something high above the rooftops.\n\n“Sir. Two o’clock, high. Do you see that?”\n\nYou squint. A tiny blinking light, hanging perfectly still in the sky.\n\n“That drone’s just hanging there.”\n\n“It is not a delivery drone, sir. Those move. This one has been in that exact spot since we came outside. It is watching the neighborhood.”\n\nYou would’ve walked right under it. You HAVE walked right under it, who knows how many times.\n\n“Good eyes, Asher.”\n\n“They are your eyes, sir. I am only borrowing one.”\n\nThe drone is way too high to reach. Time to build.\n",
