     "scene_044": {
       "title": "Magnet Boot Testing",
-      "text": "\nThe idea: powerful electromagnets in the soles of your boots, run off a power core on each ankle. Walk up to a metal wall, switch them on, and keep on walking.\n\nYou build them out of your old rain boots, the magnet coils from the Load-Bot’s forklift arms, and a LOT of wire. They’re heavy, and they look ridiculous.\n\n“Ok, Asher. Test one.”\n\nYou switch them on.\n\nCLANG!\n\nYour left foot shoots sideways and sticks to the refrigerator. Your right foot stays stuck to a steel plate on the floor. You are now doing the splits, which is something you didn’t know you could do and would really like to stop doing.\n\n“Sir, the magnets appear to be working.”\n\n“Too well! They’re working TOO WELL!”\n\nA wrench slides across the workbench and sticks to your left ankle. Then a screwdriver. Then a whole handful of bolts.\n\n“You are collecting tools at an impressive rate, sir.”\n",
+      "text": "\nThe idea: powerful electromagnets in the soles of your boots, run off a power core on each ankle. Walk up to a metal wall, switch them on, and keep on walking.\n\nYou build them out of your old rain boots, the magnet coils from the Load-Bot’s forklift arms, and a LOT of wire. They’re heavy, and they look ridiculous.\n\n“Ok, Asher. Test one.”\n\nYou switch them on.\n\nCLANG!\n\nYour left foot shoots sideways and sticks to the refrigerator. Your right foot stays stuck to a steel plate on the floor. You are now doing the splits, which is something you didn’t know you could do and would really like to stop doing.\n\n“Sir, the magnets appear to be working.”\n\n“Too well! They’re working TOO WELL!”\n\nA wrench slides across the workbench and sticks to your left ankle. Then a screwdriver. Then a whole handful of bolts.\n\n“You are collecting metal items at an impressive rate, sir.”\n",
       "choices": {
         "1": {
           "text": "Yank your foot free",
@@ -693,7 +693,7 @@
         "yanked": "\nYou pull as hard as you can. Your foot pops right out of the boot and you fall over in one sock, and the boot stays stuck to the fridge.\n",
         "cut_power": "\n“The switch on your left ankle, sir. No, the other switch.” You finally find it, and everything stuck to you clatters to the floor at once.\n"
       },
-      "text": "\nLesson learned. The magnets can’t just be ON. You need control.\n\nYou add a dial for strength, so you can stick to a wall without collecting every tool in the room. Then you add a switch you can hit by clicking your heels together, so your hands stay free. And then, just because you’re curious, you wire in a way to flip the magnets backward, so instead of pulling toward metal, they push away from it.\n\nYou stand on the steel floor plate and click your heels.\n\nBOING!\n\nYou shoot four feet straight up, yell, and land on the workbench on your rear end. You sit there for a second…and then you start laughing.\n\n“Attract and repel,” you say. “Stick to walls. Jump off metal. These are gonna change EVERYTHING.”\n\n“And their name, sir? I am ready.”\n\nYou look down at the big, clunky, wonderful boots.\n\n“The Stompers.”\n\nA pause.\n\n“Sir, that is actually a good name.”\n\n“I know! I don’t know what happened!”\n\nYou look out the garage door toward Main Street. There’s a bot on top of a bank that you owe a visit.\n",
+      "text": "\nLesson learned. The magnets can’t just be ON. You need control.\n\nYou add a dial for strength, so you can stick to a wall without collecting every tool in the room. Then you add a switch you can hit by clicking your heels together, so your hands stay free. And then, just because you’re curious, you wire in a way to flip the magnets backward, so instead of pulling toward metal, they push away from it.\n\nYou stand on the steel floor plate and click your heels.\n\nBOING!\n\nYou shoot four feet straight up, yell, and land on the workbench on your rear end. You sit there for a second…and then you start laughing.\n\n“Attract and repel,” you say. “Stick to walls. Jump off metal. These are gonna be FUN.”\n\n“And their name, sir? I am ready.”\n\nYou look down at the big, clunky, wonderful boots.\n\n“The Stompers.”\n\nA pause.\n\n“Sir, that is actually a good name.”\n\n“I know! Wait, they are ALL good names!”\n\nYou look out the garage door toward Main Street. There’s a bot on top of a bank that you owe a visit.\n",
