-      "text": "\nTHWOOM! One charged rock knocks the wheels right off one of its skates, and the bot tips sideways. You slide in under the blaster, hook the prybar under its back panel, and pop it.\n\nPull!\n\nThe Long Range Security Bot sits down, lowers its blaster, and goes still. Its visor fades from red to soft blue…and its thumb is STILL up. You decide to take that as a compliment.\n\n“Wait, sir. Do not let it go dark yet. Hold it right there.”\n\nYou keep one hand on the cable.\n\n“It is still listening. And from up here, with nothing in the way, I can finally hear what it is listening to.” His voice gets excited, which almost never happens. “Sir, it is a signal. A real one. All of the bots have been getting orders, and I can hear where they come from.”\n\nYou look out over {world_name} from the roof. All of your inventions got you here. It's time to put them to use.\n\nThe bot’s visor goes dark.\n\n“I lost it, sir. But I know which way it came from, and I know what it sounds like now. We can find it.”\n\nNo more waiting around for bots to come to you.\n",
+      "text": "\nTHWOOM! One charged rock knocks the wheels right off one of its skates, and the bot tips sideways. You slide in under the blaster, hook the prybar under its back panel, and pop it.\n\nPull!\n\nThe Long Range Security Bot sits down, lowers its blaster, and goes still. Its visor starts to fade…and its thumb is STILL up. You decide to take that as a compliment.\n\n“Wait, sir. Do not let it go dark yet. Hold it right there.”\n\nYou keep one hand on the cable.\n\n“It is still listening. And from up here, with nothing in the way, I can finally hear what it is listening to.” His voice gets excited, which almost never happens. “Sir, it is a signal. A real one. All of the bots have been getting orders, and I can hear where they come from.”\n\nYou look out over {world_name} from the roof. All of your inventions got you here. It’s time to use them to stop whoever is doing this.\n\nThe bot’s visor goes dark.\n\n“I lost it, sir. But I know which way it came from, and I know what it sounds like now. We can find it.”\n\nNo more waiting around for bots to come to you.\n",
