     "scene_055": {
       "title": "Past the Checkpoint",
-      "text": "\nThere’s a Load-Bot standing guard at the gate. This one isn’t haywire. Its eyes are a steady, calm red, the screen on its chest says GUARDING 100%, and it turns its big smiling face slowly from side to side.\n\n“That one is under direct control, sir. Not confused. Working.”\n\nYou watch it. Left. Right. Left. Right. It takes six whole seconds to turn its head all the way around.\n\n“Count me in, Asher.”\n\n“Three. Two. One. Go.”\n\nYou slip through the gate behind its back and duck between two flatbed trucks. Rows of broken bots are stacked up on either side of you, waiting their turn. Some still have their old stickers on. HAPPY HELPER. CITY PARKS DEPT. ASK ME FOR DIRECTIONS!\n\nA door opens somewhere, and a loud voice echoes across the lot.\n\n“No, no, NO! I said I wanted MORE robots going haywire on Elm Street, not FEWER! Do I have to do everything myself? Somebody get me GAS headquarters on the phone!”\n\nA tired voice answers. “Sir, you are GAS headquarters.”\n\n“Then why did nobody PICK UP?!”\n\nYou freeze against the truck. Footsteps come closer…stop…then go away again.\n\nYou count to ten, then slip through the open door.\n",
+      "text": "\nThere’s a Load-Bot standing guard at the gate. This one isn’t haywire. Its eyes are a steady, calm red, the screen on its chest says GUARDING 100%, and it turns its big smiling face slowly from side to side.\n\n“That one is under direct control, sir. Not confused. Working.”\n\nYou watch it. Left. Right. Left. Right. It takes six whole seconds to turn its head all the way around.\n\n“Count me in, Asher.”\n\n“Three. Two. One. Go.”\n\nYou slip through the gate behind its back and duck between two flatbed trucks. Rows of broken bots are stacked up on either side of you, waiting their turn. Some still have their old stickers on. HAPPY HELPER. CITY PARKS DEPT. ASK ME FOR DIRECTIONS!\n\nA door opens somewhere, and a loud voice echoes across the lot.\n\n“No, no, NO! I said I wanted MORE robots going haywire on Elm Street, not FEWER! Do I have to do everything myself? Somebody get me GAS headquarters on the phone!”\n\nA tired voice answers. “Sir, you are GAS headquarters.”\n\n“Then why didn’t I PICK UP?!”\n\nYou freeze against the truck. Footsteps come closer…stop…then go away again.\n\nYou count to ten, then slip through the open door.\n",
