     "scene_056": {
       "title": "The Side Window",
-      "text": "\nYou circle around the side of the cannery, sticking to the shadows.\n\nThere are no doors on this side, but there’s a window on the second floor with a light on and a steel drainpipe running right up next to it.\n\nClunk. Clunk. Clunk. Up you go!\n\nYou peek in. It’s an office with a huge desk, a huge chair, and a huge painting of a man in a shiny suit shaking hands with himself. Nobody’s inside.\n\nYou pry the window open with The Can Opener using the prybar, climb in, and land on carpet so thick you sink into it.\n\n“Sir, there is a computer on that desk, and it is unlocked. There is a sticky note on the screen. It says ‘Password: password.’”\n\n“He didn’t even need it. He left himself logged in.”\n\n“This is the man who has been beating us, sir?”\n\n“Let’s not tell anyone.”\n",
+      "text": "\nYou circle around the side of the cannery, sticking to the shadows.\n\nThere are no doors on this side, but there’s a window on the second floor with a light on and a steel drainpipe running right up next to it.\n\nClunk. Clunk. Clunk. Up you go!\n\nYou peek in. It’s an office with a huge desk, a huge chair, and a huge painting of a man in a shiny suit shaking hands with…himself. This guy is strange, but luckily nobody’s inside.\n\nYou pry the window open with The Can Opener using the prybar, climb in, and land on carpet so thick you sink into it.\n\n“Sir, there is a computer on that desk, and it is unlocked. There is a sticky note on the screen. It says ‘Password: password.’”\n\n“Asher, he didn’t even need it. He left himself logged in. Who is this guy?”\n\n“The man who has been beating us, sir?”\n\n“Yeah…let’s not tell anyone.”\n",
