     "scene_058": {
       "title": "The Man in the Shiny Suit",
-      "text": "\nThe next morning, there’s a little stage set up in the town square with gold balloons tied all over it.\n\nYou stand at the back of the crowd with your hood up.\n\nA man bounces up the steps. Shiny suit. Big smile. Too many teeth.\n\n“Hello, hello, HELLO, {world_name}! Max Grabs, of GAS! You know me! You love me!”\n\nNobody claps, so he claps for himself.\n\n“I have been hearing about these terrible, awful, no-good robot attacks. Who could be behind them? Nobody knows! It is a mystery! And that is why I, out of the goodness of my heart, am offering to buy every single home and business in this neighborhood. For a very fair price!”\n\nHe spreads his arms wide.\n\n“GAS is growing! GAS is everywhere! Soon, every building you see will be made by GAS!”\n\nA little kid near the front loses it completely. Max points right at him.\n\n“That’s right! Laugh with JOY!”\n\n“GAS lingers! GAS never goes away! GAS is coming to YOUR street!”\n\nSomebody’s dad, quietly: “Not if I close the windows.”\n\nMax spots a face he knows.\n\n“Mr. Lin! Great guy! You’d sell to GAS, wouldn’t you?”\n\nMr. Lin doesn’t stand up. “I’d sell you a fan.”\n\nThe whole square laughs. Max beams and claps his hands together.\n\n“I’ll take TWO!”\n\nHe reaches for his note cards and drops them, and they scatter all over the stage. He picks one up and reads it.\n\n“‘Do not mention the antenna.’ Ha ha! Ignore that! That one’s not for you!”\n\nNear the front, Mrs. Ruiz folds her arms.\n\nStanding behind the stage, still as statues, are two Security Bots with steady red eyes. One of them is giving the crowd a thumbs-up.\n\n“That is him, sir,” Asher says in your ear.\n\n“Yeah,” you whisper. “That’s him.”\n\nPeople around you are starting to mutter, and some of them look tired enough to say yes.\n\nThis ends tonight.\n\nOn your way out of the square, Mr. Lin passes you without looking over.\n\n“Don’t blow yourself up, kid.”\n\n“The only one that is going to blow up is GAS.”\n\nHe smiles.\n",
+      "text": "\nThe next morning, there’s a little stage set up in the town square with gold balloons tied all over it.\n\nYou stand at the back of the crowd with your hood up.\n\nA man bounces up the steps. Shiny suit. Big smile. Too many teeth.\n\n“Hello, hello, HELLO, {world_name}! Max Grabs, of GAS! You know me! You love me!”\n\nNobody claps, so he claps for himself and bows.\n\n“I have been hearing about these terrible, awful, no-good robot attacks. Who could be behind them? Nobody knows! It is a mystery! And that is why I, out of the goodness of my heart, am offering to buy every single home and business in this neighborhood. For a very fair price!”\n\nHe spreads his arms wide.\n\n“GAS is growing! GAS is everywhere! Soon, every building you see will be made by GAS!”\n\nA little kid near the front loses it completely. Max points right at him.\n\n“That’s right! Laugh with JOY!”\n\n“GAS lingers! GAS never goes away! GAS is coming to YOUR street!”\n\nSomebody’s dad, quietly: “Not if I close the windows.”\n\nMax spots a face he knows.\n\n“Mr. Lin! Great guy! You’d sell to GAS, wouldn’t you?”\n\nMr. Lin doesn’t stand up. “I’d sell you a fan.”\n\nThe whole square laughs. Max beams and claps his hands together.\n\n“I’ll take TWO!”\n\nHe reaches for his note cards and drops them, and they scatter all over the stage. He picks one up and reads it.\n\n“‘Do not mention the antenna.’ Ha ha! Ignore that! That one’s not for you!”\n\nNear the front, Mrs. Ruiz folds her arms.\n\nStanding behind the stage, still as statues, are two Security Bots with steady red eyes. One of them is giving the crowd a thumbs-up.\n\n“That is him, sir,” Asher says in your ear.\n\n“Yeah,” you whisper. “That’s him.”\n\nPeople around you are starting to mutter, and some of them look tired enough to say yes.\n\nThis ends tonight.\n\nOn your way out of the square, Mr. Lin passes you without looking over.\n\n“Don’t blow yourself up, kid.”\n\n“There is only going to be one explosion. A GAS explosion.”\n\nHe smiles.\n",
