     "scene_064": {
       "title": "Confrontation",
-      "text": "\nMax Grabs is standing on a metal walkway above the big machine. He’s wearing a gold bathrobe over his shiny suit, and he’s holding a remote control with exactly one button on it.\n\n“So YOU are the little pest who has been breaking my robots! Do you know how much those cost? Almost nothing! But it is the PRINCIPLE!”\n\nHe sweeps his arm out over the machine.\n\n“Behold! The Robot Improver 3! One signal, and every rusty robot in this dump goes absolutely bananas! Prices go down! I swoop in! Everybody sells! It is the perfect plan, and nobody can prove a thing!”\n\n“What happened to 1 and 2?”\n\n“There is no 1 and 2! Three sounds BETTER!”\n\n“You kept a list,” you say. “It was called MY SECRET PLAN. That's the proof.”\n\n“But it is SECRET! It says so right in the name!”\n\nHe keeps going. Now he’s telling you all about the fountain he wants to build in Grabs Grand Plaza. It’s going to be shaped like him.\n\nWhile he talks, you look past him.\n\nBehind the walkway, at the heart of the machine, is a wall of glowing terminals. The control tower. Every cable in the building runs into it.\n\nYou crouch behind the steel pillar and open The Can Opener’s power housing. The spent core comes out hot. You set it on the floor, pull the spare from the pouch on your belt, and click it into place. A blue glow creeps back into the coils. Your strongest core. Fully charged. You’ve never dared to let all of one out at once. It would drain the tool completely.\n\nYou think about every eye light you’ve watched fade from angry red to soft blue.\n",
+      "text": "\nMax Grabs is standing on a metal walkway above the big machine. He’s wearing a gold bathrobe over his shiny suit, and he’s holding a remote control with exactly one button on it.\n\n“So YOU are the little pest who has been breaking my robots! Do you know how much those cost? Almost nothing! But it is the PRINCIPLE!”\n\nHe sweeps his arm out over the machine.\n\n“Behold! The Robot Improver 3! One signal, and every rusty robot in this dump goes absolutely bananas! Prices go down! I swoop in! Everybody sells! It is the perfect plan, and nobody can prove a thing!”\n\n“What happened to 1 and 2?”\n\n“There is no 1 and 2! Three sounds BETTER!”\n\n“You kept a list,” you say. “It was called MY SECRET PLAN. That’s the proof.”\n\n“But it is SECRET! It says so right in the name!”\n\n“Asher, I don’t think this guy is all there,” you whisper under your breath.\n\nHe keeps going. Now he’s telling you all about the fountain he wants to build in Grabs Grand Plaza. It’s going to be shaped like him.\n\nWhile he talks, you look past him.\n\nBehind the walkway, at the heart of the machine, is a wall of glowing terminals. The control tower. Every cable in the building runs into it.\n\nYou crouch behind the steel pillar and open The Can Opener’s power housing. The spent core comes out hot. You set it on the floor, pull the spare from the pouch on your belt, and click it into place. A blue glow creeps back into the coils. Your strongest core. Fully charged. You’ve never dared to let all of one out at once. It would drain the tool completely.\n\nYou think about every eye light you’ve watched fade from angry red to soft blue.\n",
