     "scene_067": {
       "title": "Police Arrive",
-      "text": "\n“Sir, the police have read your email,” Asher says. “All of it. They seem quite upset.”\n\nRed and blue lights sweep across the cannery windows, and Grabs stops mid-tantrum.\n\n“Police? Oh, wonderful! Officers! OFFICERS! Arrest this child! This is my secret robot virus machine, and that child BROKE it!”\n\nHe hears what he just said and slaps both hands over his mouth.\n\nYou’re already moving.\n\n“Asher. I need some air.”\n\n“Small window, back wall, above the crates, sir. I imagine everyone in here does.”\n\nThere’s a small window at the back of the cannery above a stack of old crates, and The Stompers have just enough charge left for one good jump.\n\nBOING!\n\nYou catch the windowsill, pull yourself up, and look back one last time. The front doors burst open. Max Grabs is standing there in one slipper and a gold bathrobe, in front of a smoking machine, with his hands up.\n\n“I would like to speak to my lawyer,” he says. “And also my mommy.”\n\nAn officer picks up the folder off the desk. Every page inside is stamped PROPERTY OF GAS. She flips through it and shakes her head.\n\n“Everything in here is GAS.”\n\nMax, sincerely: “Thank you.”\n\nYou slip out the back window and drop into the dark before anyone can stop you. You’re not doing this to get famous.\n",
